8. OPEN DESIGN TENSIONS

# Question Impact
1 Hash function choice. Same as A6 — SHA-256 vs ternary-compatible. Cross-spec consistency.
2 AOL storage location. SRAM, external flash, or both? Affects power and cost.
3 Archive protocol. How are old entries moved without breaking the chain? Needs its own spec if not trivial.
4 Checkpoint frequency. Every plan boundary? Every N steps? Affects rollback granularity and log size.
5 AOL signature cadence. Per entry, or batched? Per entry is simpler; batched saves energy. Trade-off.
6 Observation scope. Which fields go into the BWS? Deployment-specific, but standard defaults may be needed.
7 Determinism across reboots. The AOL persists; the BWS does not. How does the agent re-initialize BWS after power cycle? Needs a declared initialization.
8 Log overflow behavior. Halt, archive, or compress — which is default? Affects certification under DO-178C.

None are fatal. All must be resolved before A7 v2.0.

