APPENDIX A — Plain Language

Does the agent remember?
Yes. Every decision, every action, every failure. It's all written down.
Can it change what it wrote?
No. The past is sealed. New entries are added; old ones stay.
Can you prove nothing was changed?
Yes. Every entry has a fingerprint of the one before it. If anything changes, the chain breaks.
What about the present?
The present is a small window — the last few moments. It slides forward as new moments arrive.
Can the agent rewrite the present?
No. Only push new moments in. The window is fixed.
What if the log gets too big?
It can be archived or compressed. Never lost. Never falsified.
What is this called?
A7 — persistent deterministic memory.

